# Users module — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development):
#   dotnet user-secrets set ConnectionStrings:Portal "Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=nimi_portal;Username=postgres;Password=<password>" --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
#   dotnet user-secrets set SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL "admin@cu.edu.eg" --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
#   dotnet user-secrets set SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD "<a password>" --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
# Run:  dotnet run --project src/Hosts/Host.CairoUniversity
#   → migrations apply and the first admin is seeded (Development only). Tokens are signed with a random
#     per-run key in Development unless Auth:Jwt:SigningKey is set — restart = log in again.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminEmail = admin@cu.edu.eg
@adminPassword = paste-SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD-here

### 1. Log in as the seeded admin → copy "accessToken" into @token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2. Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Create a faculty
# @name faculty
POST {{host}}/api/admin/faculties
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "ENG", "name": "Engineering", "nameAr": "الهندسة" }

### 4. Create a department in it
# @name department
POST {{host}}/api/admin/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "facultyId": "{{faculty.response.body.$.id}}", "code": "CS", "name": "Computer Science", "nameAr": "علوم الحاسب" }

### 5. Lists (paged: ?page=1&pageSize=20)
GET {{host}}/api/faculties
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/departments?facultyId={{faculty.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Create a student → studentCode CS-2026-0001 + one-time temporaryPassword
# @name student
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "student",
  "fullName": "أحمد علي",
  "email": "ahmed@cu.edu.eg",
  "departmentId": "{{department.response.body.$.id}}",
  "enrollmentYear": 2026,
  "gender": "male"
}

### 7. Create a professor (academicTitle: professor | lecturer | demonstrator)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "professor",
  "fullName": "د. هاني",
  "email": "hany@cu.edu.eg",
  "departmentId": "{{department.response.body.$.id}}",
  "academicTitle": "professor"
}

### 8. Bulk import a cohort — multipart, field "file"; columns:
#    full_name,email,national_id,department_code,enrollment_year   (max 2,000 rows / 5 MB, UTF-8)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/bulk
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cohort

--cohort
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="cohort.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

full_name,email,national_id,department_code,enrollment_year
منى حسن,mona@cu.edu.eg,29901010000001,CS,2026
عمر سعيد,omar@cu.edu.eg,,CS,2026
--cohort--

### 9. Find users (role / facultyId / departmentId / isActive / search, paged)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users?role=student&search=CS-2026
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Deactivate / reactivate (204)
PATCH {{host}}/api/admin/users/{{student.response.body.$.user.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### 11. Admin password reset → new one-time temporaryPassword, forced change, lockout cleared
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/{{student.response.body.$.user.id}}/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. The student's first login (temporary password) → mustChangePassword: true
# @name studentLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmed@cu.edu.eg", "password": "paste-temporaryPassword-here" }

### 13. Anything else is 403 password_change_required until the password is changed
GET {{host}}/api/faculties
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 14. Change it → fresh token with mustChangePassword: false
POST {{host}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{studentLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "paste-temporaryPassword-here", "newPassword": "MyOwnPass9" }
